Source: matrix-overlay
Section: x11
# x11 is where the comparable session utilities sit (xscreensaver, waybar,
# swaylock, mako in Ubuntu's index). Section is advisory, but "graphics" reads as
# "image tool" to whoever reviews this.
# Policy 4.7.3 no longer *requires* a Priority field, but the dpkg shipped in
# Ubuntu 24.04 does not yet default it for binary stanzas: omitting it makes
# dpkg-genchanges warn and write "Priority: -" into the .changes file. Keep one
# field here (inherited by the binary stanza) until the archive tooling catches
# up - see Debian #1124443 on the upgrading-checklist wording.
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Nelson Pascoal <foomip@users.noreply.github.com>
# gcc, make and dpkg-dev come from build-essential, which every build chroot
# has; naming them unversioned is a lintian error. pkg-config is the obsolete
# name for pkgconf.
