Package: matrix-overlay
Architecture: any
# pycairo and the Pango typelib are not optional, whatever the backend: the glyph
# atlas is built with PangoCairo into Cairo ImageSurfaces and then uploaded as a
# GL texture, so the GL path needs them exactly as much as the Cairo painter does.
# The autopkgtest `smoke` entry installs this package with its Depends and no
# Recommends, and it died on `import cairo` before these two were listed here.
# Comments in control files must start at column 0: inside a field's continuation
# lines they become part of the value.
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         ${shlibs:Depends},
         python3,
         python3-gi,
         gir1.2-glib-2.0,
         python3-cairo,
         gir1.2-pango-1.0
Recommends: gir1.2-gtk-3.0,
            gir1.2-gtklayershell-0.1,
            python3-gi-cairo,
            fonts-noto-cjk
Suggests: cosmic-settings-daemon
Description: Matrix-style digital rain over every screen on COSMIC/Wayland
 A fullscreen overlay that runs The Matrix "digital rain" across every monitor
 while the desktop dims underneath. Escape, a pointer click, or the same
 shortcut brings the desktop back.
 .
 One zwlr_layer_shell_v1 OVERLAY surface is created per output and painted with
 GLES2 over EGL, so the compositor imports dmabufs instead of copying a CPU
 buffer: measured at 22 fps for about nine percent of one core on a 1080p
 laptop iGPU. The GPU that renders is chosen from the connectors that actually
 drive a connected output, which is what makes one package work on both a
 hybrid machine and a single-GPU one.
 .
 There is no window and no tray icon by design. Bind the command "matrix-rain"
 to a COSMIC custom shortcut (Settings, Keyboard, Custom shortcuts) to get the
 Ctrl+Shift+M trigger; a launcher entry is installed as well so a show can be
 started without a keybind. The configuration file is reloaded while a show is
 running, so speed, density, tail length, colours, font and glyph set can be
 tuned live.
 .
 A Cairo/GTK layer-shell painter is kept as a fallback for compositors whose GL
 path is unusable; its dependencies are Recommends rather than Depends.
